{title: Raise a Hallelujah}
{artist: Bethel Live}
{key: Db}
{tempo: 83}

{comment: Verse 1}
Verse 1 (Hold first chord first time through):
I [Db]raise a Hallelujah,   in the [Gb]presence of my enemies
I [Bbm]raise a Hallelujah,   [Ab]louder than the unbelief
I [Db]raise a Hallelujah,   my [Gb]weapon is a melody
I [Bbm]raise a Hallelujah,   [Ab]heaven comes to fight for me

{comment: Chorus}
[Gb]I'm gonna sing in the [Db]middle of the storm
[Bbm]Louder and louder, you're gonna [Ab]hear my praises roar
[Gb]Up from the ashes, [Db]hope will arise
[Bbm]Death is defeated, the [Ab]King is alive

{comment: Verse 2}
I [Db]raise a Hallelujah,   with [Gb]everything inside of me
I [Bbm]raise a Hallelujah,   [Ab]I will watch the darkness flee
I [Db]raise a Hallelujah,   in the [Gb]middle of the mystery
I [Bbm]raise a Hallelujah,   [Ab]fear you lost your hold on me

